name    topown
prog    top 3
# Plain `top' lists your own processes, busy or idle (2026-09-26).  Before,
# it listed only those that had used a tick since the last screen, so with
# nothing else running it showed its headings and, now and then, itself --
# `bash' sitting at its prompt used no ticks and never appeared.  bash is
# the line that tells the two apart.  A plain `bash' matches the prompt
# and `top' the command line -- measured: that version PASSED against the
# old binary, whose screen had headings and no rows.  So these are the
# rows themselves: bash is process 3 and top process 4 in this session,
# both 1.7 at priority 128.
rate    0.6
wait    8
snap    listed
expect  Id PId Grp.Usr Prio
expect    3   2   1.7    128
expect    4   3   1.7    128
absent  Process Aborted
wait    8
snap    refreshed
key     \003
wait    2
